01:28:23,360 --> 01:28:29,360
 I think this is a good way to set the table for the generalized goal of elevating the look and feel of the community.

1178
01:28:29,360 --> 01:28:36,360
 I understand that there are necessary concerns for being very fiscally prudent with taxpayer dollars.

1179
01:28:36,360 --> 01:28:43,360
 And at the same time, I think there are some really key things that ought to be focused on at the same time to complete it and complete it well.

1180
01:28:43,360 --> 01:28:46,360
 Or at the same time, balancing that against our fiscal constraints.

1181
01:28:46,360 --> 01:28:49,360
 I would say that if you have a plan, we'd like to see it.

1182
01:28:49,360 --> 01:28:50,360
 Yeah, absolutely.

1183
01:28:50,360 --> 01:28:54,360
 Because that at least gives us an idea of what the overall spend is going to be for it.

1184
01:28:54,360 --> 01:29:02,360
 It gives the council the opportunity to say, yes, we're on board with it or maybe not all of it, maybe these things or not at all.

1185
01:29:02,360 --> 01:29:05,360
 And I think that's important to be able to make that decision.

1186
01:29:05,360 --> 01:29:08,360
 So we're not, I agree with council member Clark.

1187
01:29:08,360 --> 01:29:13,360
 There needs to be an idea of what the end goal of this is and what the overall cost is.

1188
01:29:13,360 --> 01:29:20,360
 Because the reality is, is we're taking this money from other places that we want to make sure we're comfortable with doing that.

1189
01:29:20,360 --> 01:29:21,360
 Understood.

1190
01:29:21,360 --> 01:29:23,360
 And I will look toward that.

